          "through": null
        },
        "locator": "Current Codex task, project-owner request dated 2026-08-10",
        "reviewer": "Project owner and Economics Department domain expert",
        "sourceId": "OWNER-CONFIRMATION-DISTRIBUTION-2026-08-10",
        "sourceType": "OWNER_CONFIRMATION",
        "statement": "Balanced distributes total planner-tracked load as evenly as feasible with remainders in later usable years. Explore uses a lighter first planned year and backloads remaining work, including a 2/3/3/4 full freshman target for twelve tracked requirements. Annual and within-year targets use actual capacity after fixed Taking now courses and other reservations. Full-year preferred term shapes are 1/1/1 for three, equally preferred 1/2/1 and 2/1/1 for four, and 2/2/1 for five, with no preferred Spring/May target above one. Explore ranks 1/1/0 ahead of the other separated two-course shapes and same-term arrangements only as rescue candidates. These preferences rank academically valid plans and never change feasibility, requirements, prerequisites, offerings, capacity, or readiness.",
        "supersedes": "Earlier incomplete implementation details for Balanced remainder placement and within-year distribution"
      }
    ]
